.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-offbox-restore 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-offbox\-restore \- Put a session\*(Aqs pushed snapshot back where it was read from, in a container that does not have it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten offbox restore\fR [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-session\fR> <\fB\-\-harness\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Put a session\*(Aqs pushed snapshot back where it was read from, in a container that does not have it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fI<session>\fR
The harness\*(Aqs own identifier for the session whose state is pushed
.TP
\fB\-\-harness\fR \fI<harness>\fR
The harness the session belongs to; it selects where the session\*(Aqs records are read from
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<from>\fR
The session this one continues; its snapshot is restored when this session has none
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
